{"name":"Rush Hour","hex":"#536770","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rush hour","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The times of the day when traffic jams are commonplace, due mainly to people commuting to or from work."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rush_hour"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Rush Hour","blocks":[{"text":"The Rush Hour is a 1928 American silent comedy film directed by E. Mason Hopper and starring Marie Prevost, Harrison Ford and Seena Owen."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/The_Rush_Hour.jpg/330px-The_Rush_Hour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Rush_Hour"},{"title":"Rush Hour (1941 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Rush Hour is a 1941 British Public Information short film made by the wartime Ministry of Information and designed to pass on an important message to cinemagoers in a humorous manner. It was directed by Anthony Asquith, written by Rodney Ackland and Arthur Boys, and produced by Edward Black."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/2d/Rushhourasquith.jpg/330px-Rushhourasquith.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rush_Hour_(1941_film)"},{"title":"Rush Hour (1998 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Rush Hour is a 1998 American buddy cop action comedy film directed by Brett Ratner from a screenplay by Jim Kouf and Ross LaManna and a story by LaManna. It stars Jackie Chan, Chris Tucker, Tom Wilkinson, Chris Penn, and Elizabeth Peña. In the film, Hong Kong Police Force (HKPF) Chief Inspector Lee (Chan) and Los Angeles Police Department (LAPD) Detective James Carter (Tucker) are forced to work together to rescue a Chinese diplomat's abducted daughter."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/49/Rush_Hour_poster.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rush_Hour_(1998_film)"},{"title":"Rush hour","blocks":[{"text":"A rush hour or peak hour is a part of the day during which traffic congestion on roads and crowding on public transport is at its highest. Normally, this happens twice every weekday: once in the morning and once in the afternoon or evening, the times during which most people commute. The term is often used for a period of peak congestion that may last for more than one hour."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Standing_on_the_Yellow_Platform_Line.jpg/330px-Standing_on_the_Yellow_Platform_Line.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rush_hour"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Miami_traffic_jam%2C_I-95_North_rush_hour.jpg/500px-Miami_traffic_jam%2C_I-95_North_rush_hour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Miami_traffic_jam%2C_I-95_North_rush_hour.jpg/1280px-Miami_traffic_jam%2C_I-95_North_rush_hour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Miami_traffic_jam%2C_I-95_North_rush_hour.jpg/500px-Miami_traffic_jam%2C_I-95_North_rush_hour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Afternoon rush hour traffic on Interstate 95 in Miami","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMiami_traffic_jam%2C_I-95_North_rush_hour.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/A32_approaching_Flemington_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-A32_approaching_Flemington_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/A32_approaching_Flemington_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-A32_approaching_Flemington_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/A32_approaching_Flemington_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-A32_approaching_Flemington_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A set on the Sydney Trains network. All suburban trains on the network have two decks for increased capacity.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA32_approaching_Flemington_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Fuxingmen_Station_%28Line_2%29_Platform_20181106.jpg/500px-Fuxingmen_Station_%28Line_2%29_Platform_20181106.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Fuxingmen_Station_%28Line_2%29_Platform_20181106.jpg/1280px-Fuxingmen_Station_%28Line_2%29_Platform_20181106.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Fuxingmen_Station_%28Line_2%29_Platform_20181106.jpg/500px-Fuxingmen_Station_%28Line_2%29_Platform_20181106.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fuxingmen station transfer from Line 2 to Line 1. Note the barrier used to restrict passenger flow to reduce congestion on Line 1 platforms. ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFuxingmen_Station_(Line_2)_Platform_20181106.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Rush_hour_at_Shinjuku_02.JPG/500px-Rush_hour_at_Shinjuku_02.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Rush_hour_at_Shinjuku_02.JPG/1280px-Rush_hour_at_Shinjuku_02.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Rush_hour_at_Shinjuku_02.JPG/500px-Rush_hour_at_Shinjuku_02.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rush hour at Shinjuku Station, Tokyo. The station is the world's busiest,[10] used by approximately 3.8 million passengers per day in 2008.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARush_hour_at_Shinjuku_02.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/US_25_Gratiot_Ave_1941.jpg/500px-US_25_Gratiot_Ave_1941.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/US_25_Gratiot_Ave_1941.jpg/1280px-US_25_Gratiot_Ave_1941.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/US_25_Gratiot_Ave_1941.jpg/500px-US_25_Gratiot_Ave_1941.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Heavy rush hour congestion on US 25 along Gratiot Avenue in Detroit in the 1940s","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUS_25_Gratiot_Ave_1941.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Atlanta_75.85.jpg/500px-Atlanta_75.85.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Atlanta_75.85.jpg/1280px-Atlanta_75.85.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Atlanta_75.85.jpg/500px-Atlanta_75.85.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Traffic in Atlanta during rush hour","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAtlanta_75.85.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/I-95_SB_approaching_Girard_Avenue-Lehigh_Avenue.JPG/500px-I-95_SB_approaching_Girard_Avenue-Lehigh_Avenue.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.